# Where the API is.
#
# `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` is inlined into the bundle at build time, which is right for a
# base URL and wrong for anything secret.
#
# The default (in src/api.ts) is localhost, which works for a simulator running
# on the same machine as `php artisan serve`. A real device cannot reach your
# laptop's localhost.
#
# `pnpm run demo --lan` does the whole thing for you: it binds every server to
# all interfaces, rebuilds the web app for this machine's address, and prints
# the exact line to put below. Writing it by hand works too — the address is
# this machine's on the network, and the API has to be serving on all
# interfaces (`php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0`) or the phone is refused.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000/api
